# Task E01/F01/US02/T01 (ADR-007: remote state per environment, HCP
# Terraform workspaces raffa-dev / raffa-demo). HCP Terraform packages
# the contents of a configuration directory and uploads it for every
# VCS-driven or CLI-driven ("terraform plan/apply" run via a remote
# workspace) run. Nothing that could let local state, a local backend
# override, or a real credential ride along in that upload belongs here --
# state and secrets live only in HCP Terraform / Key Vault, never in a
# file that could be packaged or committed.
#
# infra/environments/{dev,demo}/ do not exist yet (feature-02 owns the
# module layout from ADR-007). Once they do, mirror this file into each of
# them too: Terraform resolves .terraformignore relative to the actual
# configuration directory being packaged for a given run, not just this
# infra/ root.

# Local state -- must never exist on disk here; HCP Terraform is the only
# state store (ADR-007). A stray local statefile must never be uploaded.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl

# Local backend / CLI overrides -- every backend is remote (HCP Terraform
# workspace per environment); a local override.tf could otherwise redirect
# state or providers out from under that guarantee.
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# Variable files may carry environment-specific (sometimes sensitive)
# values; keep them out of the uploaded package by default.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!example.tfvars

# Workstation noise that must never leave the workstation.
crash.log
crash.*.log
.DS_Store
